1
00:00:05,980 --> 00:00:09,000
YAMU! YAMU! YAMU! YAMU!

2
00:00:30,440 --> 00:00:31,400
Your moves!

3
00:01:07,400 --> 00:01:09,106
What do you think's in there?

4
00:01:09,560 --> 00:01:11,619
Well, hopefully the Pharaoh's name.

5
00:01:12,860 --> 00:01:13,690
Tristan!

6
00:01:13,820 --> 00:01:15,996
That room might be filled with traps!

7
00:01:18,740 --> 00:01:21,152
Looks more like it's filled with nothing.

8
00:01:21,380 --> 00:01:25,637
Yeah, but Grandpa said things in this
tomb aren't always what they appear to be.

9
00:01:25,720 --> 00:01:27,040
Then what are they?

10
00:01:27,840 --> 00:01:32,180
He just means that sometimes you have
to look beyond the obvious. Right!

11
00:01:32,420 --> 00:01:33,340
Now let's look!

12
00:01:34,140 --> 00:01:36,100
I'm looking, I'm looking!

13
00:01:36,420 --> 00:01:37,479
Well, look harder.

14
00:01:37,940 --> 00:01:39,200
I found a clue.

15
00:01:39,460 --> 00:01:40,480
You show off.

16
00:01:40,960 --> 00:01:42,100
Where is it?

17
00:01:42,420 --> 00:01:44,800
You're standing on it. Huh?

18
00:01:45,140 --> 00:01:47,100
He's right! Check it out!

19
00:01:47,520 --> 00:01:50,696
Yeah, but once again, it's
written in chicken scratch.

20
00:01:50,900 --> 00:01:55,665
It says, he who solves the Millennium
Puzzle must return the wish he was granted.

21
00:01:56,280 --> 00:01:58,380
Only then is he able to pass.

22
00:01:58,900 --> 00:02:01,300
Since when can you read hieroglyphics?

23
00:02:01,480 --> 00:02:04,245
There's a lot about me
you don't know, Wheeler.

24
00:02:04,400 --> 00:02:06,576
So if you expect to save the pharaoh,

25
00:02:06,700 --> 00:02:09,617
you better give back whatever
it is the puzzle gave to you.

26
00:02:09,700 --> 00:02:12,935
But Tristan, what you're
saying doesn't make any sense.

27
00:02:13,140 --> 00:02:16,417
The wish that was granted to me by
my puzzle can never be given back.

28
00:02:16,500 --> 00:02:17,441
It's impossible.

29
00:02:19,260 --> 00:02:24,257
The age of darkness is upon us,
and our kingdom needs a new leader.

30
00:02:24,340 --> 00:02:26,240
You set home.

31
00:02:27,300 --> 00:02:28,620
Where am I?

32
00:02:28,780 --> 00:02:30,760
With me, where you belong.

33
00:02:31,260 --> 00:02:33,080
Now rise, my son.

34
00:02:34,520 --> 00:02:39,500
A new pharaoh deserves the
power of a new Egyptian god.

35
00:02:39,840 --> 00:02:43,760
And as we speak, a messenger
comes bearing this gift.

36
00:02:44,480 --> 00:02:49,600
Only after you've accepted her offering
can you serve as the new king of Egypt.

37
00:02:54,920 --> 00:02:55,780
Kisara!

38
00:02:56,500 --> 00:02:57,360
Yes!

39
00:02:57,760 --> 00:03:00,160
That girl holds the key to the throne!

40
00:03:00,640 --> 00:03:03,240
And you must take it from her!

41
00:03:04,560 --> 00:03:05,420
Seto!

42
00:03:17,780 --> 00:03:18,640
Seto!

43
00:03:20,300 --> 00:03:21,160
Kisara!

44
00:03:21,680 --> 00:03:22,800
It's you!

45
00:03:24,540 --> 00:03:26,320
I knew I'd find you!

46
00:03:26,860 --> 00:03:28,801
It isn't safe for you to be here.

47
00:03:29,020 --> 00:03:32,255
You saved my life the night
your village was destroyed.

48
00:03:32,420 --> 00:03:34,560
Now it's my turn to save you.

49
00:03:35,460 --> 00:03:37,100
You needn't do this.

50
00:03:39,260 --> 00:03:40,840
It's that guy again.

51
00:03:43,680 --> 00:03:45,800
Don't be fooled by her innocence.

52
00:03:46,140 --> 00:03:49,022
She wields a mighty creature
that belongs to you.

53
00:03:49,440 --> 00:03:50,480
Now take it!

54
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:51,830
Seto, please.

55
00:03:52,080 --> 00:03:54,256
You mustn't listen to a word he says.

56
00:03:59,100 --> 00:04:01,220
Zork's resurrection has begun.

57
00:04:01,580 --> 00:04:03,080
You must act swiftly.

58
00:04:03,560 --> 00:04:07,380
Now use your Millennium Rod to
seize the White Dragon, my son.

59
00:04:07,760 --> 00:04:13,060
I am not your son, for my father left me
when he pledged his loyalty to the Shadows.

60
00:04:13,780 --> 00:04:15,860
Let us go, Kisara. Yes.

61
00:04:17,480 --> 00:04:22,460
How dare you disrespect me
after all I've done for you?

62
00:04:24,600 --> 00:04:25,820
We're trapped!

63
00:04:28,360 --> 00:04:29,820
Not for long.

64
00:04:33,220 --> 00:04:34,980
Now set us free!

65
00:04:38,860 --> 00:04:40,780
You'll never escape!

66
00:04:47,160 --> 00:04:49,800
You're no match for me, Seto!

67
00:04:50,580 --> 00:04:52,060
Is that so?

68
00:04:55,760 --> 00:04:58,200
You leave me no choice!

69
00:05:02,800 --> 00:05:03,630
No!

70
00:05:07,620 --> 00:05:08,450
Seto!

71
00:05:08,620 --> 00:05:12,640
If you won't take her power, then I will!

72
00:05:16,280 --> 00:05:19,400
Surrender your power to my son at once!

73
00:05:28,220 --> 00:05:30,980
Behold your destiny, Seto!

74
00:05:31,280 --> 00:05:32,580
Be careful, Kisara.

75
00:05:33,740 --> 00:05:36,200
My blue-eyes white dragon.

76
00:05:39,220 --> 00:05:40,540
That sound!

77
00:05:40,960 --> 00:05:42,740
I'm coming, Seto!

78
00:05:54,780 --> 00:05:55,610
Kisara!

79
00:05:59,460 --> 00:06:00,340
Not so fast!

80
00:06:04,140 --> 00:06:06,100
Your fate is sealed!

81
00:06:07,500 --> 00:06:09,400
Sealed in stone, that is!

82
00:06:17,340 --> 00:06:18,880
You mustn't do this.

83
00:06:19,020 --> 00:06:21,097
You no longer have the strength to fight.

84
00:06:21,180 --> 00:06:22,877
I know what I'm doing. Do you?

85
00:06:22,960 --> 00:06:27,740
No matter what it takes, I won't
allow him to hurt you, Seto. Hurt him?

86
00:06:27,880 --> 00:06:29,277
Haven't you been listening?

87
00:06:29,360 --> 00:06:33,660
I plan to transform him into the
most powerful king that ever lived!

88
00:06:33,820 --> 00:06:34,900
But at what cost?

89
00:06:35,040 --> 00:06:38,000
So I can become like
you, a puppet of Zork?

90
00:06:39,200 --> 00:06:41,494
Kisara has helped me realize something.

91
00:06:41,660 --> 00:06:44,837
I would sooner be a peasant
in a world still shining with

92
00:06:44,920 --> 00:06:48,460
hope than a pharaoh in a world
contaminated by darkness.

93
00:06:49,200 --> 00:06:50,340
You mean that?

94
00:06:50,860 --> 00:06:54,920
So you're choosing this riffraff
over your own flesh and blood?

95
00:06:55,400 --> 00:06:59,260
I brought you into this world and
I have the power to remove you!

96
00:07:00,060 --> 00:07:03,560
The part of you that was
once my father is long gone!

97
00:07:04,100 --> 00:07:06,820
And now I see what's
been left in his place.

98
00:07:07,080 --> 00:07:09,727
A weak old man with a
heart full of darkness.

99
00:07:10,660 --> 00:07:11,490
ZETO!

100
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:20,120
No, Kasara!

101
00:07:24,640 --> 00:07:27,560
Kassara, please wake up. I'm sorry.

102
00:07:27,920 --> 00:07:29,180
It's not your fault.

103
00:07:34,040 --> 00:07:38,380
I knew if I took aim at you, that
fool would try to protect you.

104
00:07:38,940 --> 00:07:41,620
Believe me, it was for your own good.

105
00:07:42,020 --> 00:07:47,437
Now you and I can use her power to
rule the new world as father and son.

106
00:07:47,520 --> 00:07:51,300
One mind, one body, one king!

107
00:07:51,800 --> 00:07:52,859
That's right, son.

108
00:07:53,040 --> 00:07:57,000
Come and stand by my side,
so our spirits may unite.

109
00:07:57,300 --> 00:07:58,600
I'll never join you.

110
00:08:11,060 --> 00:08:12,180
It's Yugi.

111
00:08:13,020 --> 00:08:13,850
Seto!

112
00:08:16,340 --> 00:08:17,460
Are you all right?

113
00:08:18,340 --> 00:08:20,458
We've been waiting for you, Pharaoh.

114
00:08:20,660 --> 00:08:23,040
After all, Zork's arrival is upon us.

115
00:08:23,800 --> 00:08:27,640
And he deserves to be greeted by
a king worthy of his greatness.

116
00:08:28,180 --> 00:08:30,121
Seto, what are you talking about?

117
00:08:33,420 --> 00:08:34,860
What happened to her?

118
00:08:36,380 --> 00:08:38,480
Her creature was sealed in stone!

119
00:08:38,880 --> 00:08:40,260
I know who did this!

120
00:08:40,460 --> 00:08:42,000
Tell me where Agnodon is!

121
00:08:42,120 --> 00:08:43,080
Right here!

122
00:08:50,480 --> 00:08:51,310
Surprise!

123
00:08:51,393 --> 00:08:53,600
I've infiltrated Zitto's mind!

124
00:08:56,760 --> 00:09:00,720
My son was having difficulty
accepting his destiny, you see.

125
00:09:01,040 --> 00:09:05,220
So I decided to help him make
up his mind by taking it over.

126
00:09:07,220 --> 00:09:10,357
The time has finally arrived, Zitto!

127
00:09:10,440 --> 00:09:13,040
The power of the White Dragon is yours!

128
00:09:13,480 --> 00:09:16,009
Now destroy the pharaoh
and take his place!

129
00:09:16,400 --> 00:09:17,230
Let's duel!

130
00:09:20,360 --> 00:09:21,920
Seto, don't do this!

131
00:09:22,060 --> 00:09:24,354
Your mind has been clouded by darkness!

132
00:09:24,780 --> 00:09:25,610
Wrong!

133
00:09:25,693 --> 00:09:27,773
For the first time, everything is clear!

134
00:09:27,980 --> 00:09:29,480
Come forth, White Dragon!

135
00:09:43,420 --> 00:09:45,520
I have no choice but to fight!

136
00:09:45,780 --> 00:09:48,800
I summon Mahad, the Dark Magician!

137
00:09:52,380 --> 00:09:57,160
Prepare to feel the power of
two generations in one attack!

138
00:09:57,520 --> 00:09:58,577
He's right, Pharaoh.

139
00:09:58,660 --> 00:10:00,719
Their magic is twice as strong now.

140
00:10:01,320 --> 00:10:04,560
Now, my dragon, attack
with white lightning!

141
00:10:05,140 --> 00:10:06,640
Dark magic attack!

142
00:10:11,700 --> 00:10:13,300
Good luck, my king!

143
00:10:16,940 --> 00:10:18,380
No, Mahad!

144
00:10:18,660 --> 00:10:20,960
Your reign ends now, Pharaoh!

145
00:10:21,420 --> 00:10:24,891
You've disgraced the throne of
Egypt just like your father!

146
00:10:25,460 --> 00:10:27,300
But not for long!

147
00:10:27,720 --> 00:10:31,700
Because I'm about to take what
was meant to be mine ages ago!

148
00:10:32,520 --> 00:10:33,977
Serto, listen to me!

149
00:10:34,060 --> 00:10:38,531
Your mind is being controlled, and if
you don't break free, Egypt is doomed.

150
00:10:38,780 --> 00:10:41,480
You made a vow to protect
our land, remember?

151
00:10:41,900 --> 00:10:44,360
And I am protecting our land.

152
00:10:44,540 --> 00:10:45,460
From you!

153
00:10:45,840 --> 00:10:47,500
Now, Blue Eyes, attack!

154
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:52,660
No, please, don't.

155
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:56,830
What?

156
00:10:56,913 --> 00:10:59,720
How dare you disobey me? Attack!

157
00:11:00,380 --> 00:11:02,440
Do you hear me? I said attack!

158
00:11:05,840 --> 00:11:07,640
Thank you, Kisara.

159
00:11:10,700 --> 00:11:12,860
What is the meaning of this?

160
00:11:14,220 --> 00:11:16,280
The White Dragon!

161
00:11:20,200 --> 00:11:21,640
But how?

162
00:11:25,240 --> 00:11:26,200
Sato!

163
00:11:34,060 --> 00:11:38,380
You're free now, and I promise
Akhenaten will never harm you again.

164
00:11:40,060 --> 00:11:42,560
My power rests with you now.

165
00:11:50,680 --> 00:11:51,510
Tessara!

166
00:11:56,740 --> 00:11:59,880
Your spirit now lives
within the White Dragon.

167
00:12:07,180 --> 00:12:08,260
Nice outfit.

168
00:12:09,240 --> 00:12:12,040
Kaiba, but what are you
doing in this world?

169
00:12:12,480 --> 00:12:15,417
Don't you think I've been
asking myself the same question?

170
00:12:15,500 --> 00:12:18,057
Because I certainly didn't
choose to come here.

171
00:12:18,140 --> 00:12:21,557
Believe me, I can think of better
vacation spots than this dump.

172
00:12:21,640 --> 00:12:24,537
Now why don't you explain to me why
everyone's running around in these

173
00:12:24,620 --> 00:12:28,557
ridiculous costumes and speaking like
they're in some bad Shakespearean play?

174
00:12:28,640 --> 00:12:29,470
And him.

175
00:12:29,560 --> 00:12:33,031
Am I supposed to believe that's
some ancient version of me?

176
00:12:33,680 --> 00:12:38,700
His name is Seto, and 5,000 years ago, he
fought bravely by my side to save Egypt.

177
00:12:39,040 --> 00:12:42,580
I also learned that his father
and my father were brothers.

178
00:12:43,380 --> 00:12:45,086
Are you saying we're cousins?

179
00:12:45,240 --> 00:12:47,637
All I know is that
we've gone back in time.

180
00:12:47,720 --> 00:12:52,014
And the same evil force that once
tried to destroy mankind has come back.

181
00:12:52,100 --> 00:12:53,900
Now I suggest you go home.

182
00:12:54,220 --> 00:12:57,120
It isn't safe for you or
anyone else to be here.

183
00:12:57,360 --> 00:13:01,617
You may buy into the delusion that
you're some hotshot pharaoh, but I don't.

184
00:13:01,700 --> 00:13:06,780
And pharaoh or no pharaoh, no one tells
Seto Kaiba what to do, is that clear?

185
00:13:07,480 --> 00:13:08,600
As you wish.

186
00:13:09,560 --> 00:13:11,736
Well, you've made quite the comeback.

187
00:13:11,920 --> 00:13:15,800
But there's nothing you or the
Kaiba twins can do to stop me now.

188
00:13:16,120 --> 00:13:18,237
Looks like it's too little too late.

189
00:13:18,320 --> 00:13:21,202
In a matter of moments,
the Dark One will return.

190
00:13:22,160 --> 00:13:23,042
Bakura's right.

191
00:13:23,220 --> 00:13:25,926
As soon as the sands of
his hourglass run out,

192
00:13:26,060 --> 00:13:28,797
Zork will rise and the world
will be shrouded in darkness.

193
00:13:28,880 --> 00:13:32,337
Our only hope is to
unlock my hidden powers by

194
00:13:32,420 --> 00:13:35,380
uncovering the greatest
kept secret of my past.

195
00:13:36,080 --> 00:13:37,320
My true name.

196
00:13:39,660 --> 00:13:42,484
Thinking of a last minute
plan to win this game?

197
00:13:42,740 --> 00:13:44,420
You're wasting your time.

198
00:13:44,800 --> 00:13:46,200
I'm afraid I disagree.

199
00:13:46,800 --> 00:13:48,417
You said it yourself, Bakura.

200
00:13:48,500 --> 00:13:49,580
This is a game.

201
00:13:49,920 --> 00:13:52,567
And every challenge in
a game has a solution.

202
00:13:53,260 --> 00:13:57,300
Now need I remind you, you're
playing with the king of games.

203
00:13:57,840 --> 00:13:59,400
So let's review the clues.

204
00:13:59,880 --> 00:14:04,540
5,000 years ago, I locked Zork's
spirit away, along with my own,

205
00:14:04,820 --> 00:14:06,660
using my name as the key.

206
00:14:07,260 --> 00:14:11,480
Then, as a safety measure,
I erased my own mind. Yes,

207
00:14:11,680 --> 00:14:15,077
and unless your memory miraculously
returns in the next few moments,

208
00:14:15,160 --> 00:14:16,631
you lose the Shadow Game.

209
00:14:17,240 --> 00:14:21,537
There is, of course, another way for you
to unlock this mystery you're looking for,

210
00:14:21,620 --> 00:14:25,267
but I've already taken measures
to make sure it never happens.

211
00:14:25,720 --> 00:14:28,426
It involves those
meddlesome friends of yours.

212
00:14:28,580 --> 00:14:29,874
What about my friends?

213
00:14:30,100 --> 00:14:33,100
Let's just say they've
stumbled upon your old tomb,

214
00:14:33,240 --> 00:14:35,887
within which is inscribed
your original name.

215
00:14:36,160 --> 00:14:37,697
Why are you telling me this?

216
00:14:37,780 --> 00:14:39,517
If I give you a glimmer of hope,

217
00:14:39,600 --> 00:14:43,217
you'll be that much more devastated
when it comes crumbling down.

218
00:14:43,300 --> 00:14:45,577
You see, the moment they
discover your true name,

219
00:14:45,660 --> 00:14:48,720
their excursion will be cut
short by my newest pawn.

220
00:14:49,160 --> 00:14:50,925
And who is this pawn of yours?

221
00:14:51,120 --> 00:14:53,480
Oh, I believe you know him quite well.

222
00:14:54,100 --> 00:14:58,688
As a matter of fact, he was a faithful
friend of yours until he lost his mind.

223
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:01,920
Just tell us already, will ya?

224
00:15:02,120 --> 00:15:06,357
What was it you wished for the day you
first solved the Millennium Puzzle?

225
00:15:06,440 --> 00:15:07,700
For true friends.

226
00:15:08,760 --> 00:15:10,480
And my wish was granted.

227
00:15:11,620 --> 00:15:12,540
Aw, man.

228
00:15:12,760 --> 00:15:13,936
You win again, Yugi.

229
00:15:14,660 --> 00:15:16,480
Leave this punk to me, Yugi.

230
00:15:17,260 --> 00:15:19,160
Hey, long time no see.

231
00:15:20,280 --> 00:15:21,477
You were my wish.

232
00:15:21,560 --> 00:15:22,840
You mean that?

233
00:15:22,980 --> 00:15:23,860
It was us?

234
00:15:24,060 --> 00:15:25,620
You never told us that.

235
00:15:25,900 --> 00:15:26,760
How precious.

236
00:15:31,420 --> 00:15:33,060
Tristan! What's the deal?

237
00:15:36,640 --> 00:15:37,860
Are you nuts?

238
00:15:38,080 --> 00:15:39,433
What's gotten into you?

239
00:15:39,720 --> 00:15:41,680
Something very powerful.

240
00:15:55,720 --> 00:15:56,560
No way!

241
00:16:04,020 --> 00:16:04,850
It's simple.

242
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:08,017
Go through that door and you'll
find what you're looking for.

243
00:16:08,100 --> 00:16:10,997
But to get in there, Yugi's
got to give up his wish.

244
00:16:11,080 --> 00:16:14,845
So when he leaves this balance
beam, we leave his life for good.

245
00:16:16,560 --> 00:16:18,200
Do what you gotta do, Yugi.

246
00:16:18,820 --> 00:16:20,200
I can't do that!

247
00:16:20,480 --> 00:16:23,304
If I leave, you'll fall
into the Pit of Shadows!

248
00:16:24,080 --> 00:16:25,800
You are so pathetic!

249
00:16:26,100 --> 00:16:28,937
You finally have the chance
to find the Pharaoh's name,

250
00:16:29,020 --> 00:16:31,137
and you're worried about these two fools?

251
00:16:31,220 --> 00:16:32,050
Back off!

252
00:16:32,140 --> 00:16:33,080
As you wish!

253
00:16:40,560 --> 00:16:41,390
Yugi!

254
00:16:41,620 --> 00:16:44,000
This thing's going down! Run for it!

255
00:16:48,500 --> 00:16:49,400
Let's go!

256
00:16:56,360 --> 00:16:58,460
I guess it's true what they say.

257
00:16:58,780 --> 00:17:01,486
You gotta hang on to
your friends, right, pal?

258
00:17:04,260 --> 00:17:05,090
Hurry!

259
00:17:08,100 --> 00:17:09,800
Joey! Grab on!

260
00:17:12,060 --> 00:17:15,100
Talk about living on the edge. Let's go.

261
00:17:15,340 --> 00:17:16,340
It's good to me.

262
00:17:20,820 --> 00:17:22,720
Whoa, check it out.

263
00:17:25,100 --> 00:17:27,200
That must be the pharaoh's name.

264
00:17:27,580 --> 00:17:29,140
Yeah, but what's it say?

265
00:17:29,500 --> 00:17:33,300
It says, bird, rock, lamb, chop,
bird, bird and a bigger bird.

266
00:17:34,180 --> 00:17:35,700
Eh, so what's that mean?

267
00:17:36,100 --> 00:17:37,760
Just memorize the symbols.

268
00:17:39,080 --> 00:17:40,160
Now let's go.

269
00:17:40,800 --> 00:17:43,388
We have to find Tristan
and get out of here.

270
00:17:45,160 --> 00:17:46,920
Tristan, you in here?

271
00:17:48,640 --> 00:17:49,470
Tristan?

272
00:17:51,940 --> 00:17:54,457
I thought you three
were down for the count,

273
00:17:54,540 --> 00:17:56,817
but apparently you
don't know when to quit.

274
00:17:56,900 --> 00:17:57,730
That's it.

275
00:17:57,820 --> 00:17:59,957
Consider this friendship over, Tristan.

276
00:18:00,040 --> 00:18:01,511
I don't think that's him.

277
00:18:01,800 --> 00:18:03,506
How right you are, my friend.

278
00:18:05,680 --> 00:18:07,600
I should have known. Akura!

279
00:18:08,780 --> 00:18:10,700
Now the real fun can start.

280
00:18:13,080 --> 00:18:16,797
Unfortunately, we're unable to see
what goes on in that tomb of yours.

281
00:18:16,880 --> 00:18:18,600
But if I had to guess,

282
00:18:18,840 --> 00:18:20,637
I'd say your friends were sent plummeting

283
00:18:20,720 --> 00:18:23,485
into the shadows at the
hands of my other half.

284
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:26,840
They may even have
located your name first.

285
00:18:27,100 --> 00:18:31,100
But sadly, that information will
never make its way to you, Pharaoh.

286
00:18:31,340 --> 00:18:32,220
Oh, yes.

287
00:18:32,560 --> 00:18:34,400
Did I mention that time is up?

288
00:18:35,580 --> 00:18:36,410
No!

289
00:18:51,020 --> 00:18:51,850
Now what?

290
00:18:52,020 --> 00:18:54,902
The Dark One is about to
make his grand entrance.

291
00:18:55,120 --> 00:18:56,500
We have to stop him!

292
00:18:57,300 --> 00:18:58,130
Impossible.

293
00:18:58,260 --> 00:19:00,907
We both know there's
only one way to do that.

294
00:19:01,220 --> 00:19:04,917
And there's no way you're leaving
here with the Pharaoh's name.

295
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:06,540
I'll make sure of it.

296
00:19:07,260 --> 00:19:09,520
He's got a duel disk! Yes.

297
00:19:09,780 --> 00:19:12,440
Now prepare yourself for your final duel!

298
00:19:46,880 --> 00:19:48,234
Thank you for listening.
